;; CLI dev config — deliberately SEPARATE from the canonical /clj-kondo.edn.
;;
;; Speclj forms aren't linted — `:lint-as clojure.core/comment` skips them.
;; Trade-off: no kondo coverage inside specs, but no false positives from
;; describe/context/it/should* argument shapes. Replace with proper hooks
;; if test coverage from kondo becomes worth the effort.
;;
;; Security escalations: the blocking security linters from the plugin's
;; canonical config (`:type-mismatch` / `:refer-all` → :error) are adopted —
;; they are clean on the CLI sources. The plugin's advisory surfacing linters
;; (`:unused-binding` / `:shadowed-var` / `:unused-private-var` → :warning) are
;; intentionally NOT adopted here: `bb lint` fails on any clj-kondo warning
;; (exit 2), and the CLI has ~13 pre-existing clojure.core shadows on common
;; local names (key, name, bytes, ref, val, …). Escalating them would either
;; break the lint gate or force a sprawling, risky rename across CLI sources.
{:lint-as {speclj.core/describe   clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/context    clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/it         clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/before     clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/before-all clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/after      clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/after-all  clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/around     clojure.core/comment
           speclj.core/with       clojure.core/def
           speclj.core/with-all   clojure.core/def}

 :linters {:type-mismatch {:level :error}
           :refer-all     {:level :error}}}
